---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Bug1 = `local score = 95

if score >= 60 then
    print("D")
elseif score >= 70 then
    print("C")
elseif score >= 80 then
    print("B")
elseif score >= 90 then
    print("A")
else
    print("F")
end`;

const Bug2 = `local temp = 85

if temp > 80 then
    print("Hot")
end

if temp > 60 then
    print("Warm")
end

if temp > 40 then
    print("Cool")
end`;

const Bug3 = `local key = "x"

if key == "a" or "d" then
    print("moving")
end`;

const Bug4 = `local total = 50

if total < 50 then
    print("Shipping: 6.00")
else
    print("Free shipping")
end

if total <= 50 then
    print("You just missed free shipping!")
end`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp-lua/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Debug Challenge: Decisions</h1>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>Objective</h2>

          <p>
            Four short programs about decisions, each with exactly one thing
            wrong. <b class="text-sn-theme">All four run perfectly and all four
            are wrong.</b>
          </p>

          <p>
            Not one of them produces an error message. Two of them even produce
            output that looks reasonable until you check it against what the
            program was supposed to say.
          </p>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="bugs">
          <h2>The Four Programs</h2>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Bug 1</h3>

          <p>
            This should report a letter grade. A score of 95 prints{" "}
            <code>D</code>.
          </p>

          <Code code={Bug1} frame="code" lang="lua" title="Bug 1" class="mb-3" />

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Bug 2</h3>

          <p>
            This should describe the temperature in one word. At 85 it prints
            three lines.
          </p>

          <Code code={Bug2} frame="code" lang="lua" title="Bug 2" class="mb-3" />

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Bug 3</h3>

          <p>
            This should move only when the key is <code>a</code> or{" "}
            <code>d</code>. It prints <code>moving</code> for{" "}
            <b class="text-sn-theme">every key, including <code>x</code></b>.
          </p>

          <Code code={Bug3} frame="code" lang="lua" title="Bug 3" class="mb-3" />

          <p class="text-body-secondary">
            This one is worth more thought than the others. Nothing here is a
            typo.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Bug 4</h3>

          <p>
            An order of exactly $50 should get free shipping and nothing else.
            It prints the free shipping line <b>and</b> the missed-it line.
          </p>

          <Code code={Bug4} frame="code" lang="lua" title="Bug 4" class="mb-3" />
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>For each program, give:</p>

          <ul>
            <li>One sentence on what was wrong</li>
            <li>The corrected line, or lines, of code</li>
            <li>
              For bug 3 only: <b>what the condition is actually asking</b>
            </li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            <b class="text-sn-theme">Trace them on paper.</b> Pick a value,
            follow it line by line, and write down what each condition
            evaluates to. That is the same skill the exam's trace questions
            want.
          </p>

          <p>Worth <b>5 points</b>, graded on completion.</p>
        </section>

        <h1
          class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
        >
          Commence Debugging
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
